ote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Witty","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11053","person_slug":"sarah-witty","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sharon Claydon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10805","person_slug":"sharon-claydon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sophie Scamps","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10989","person_slug":"sophie-scamps","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Georganas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"no"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tania Lawrence","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10981","person_slug":"tania-lawrence","vote":"no"},{"name":"Terry Young","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10933","person_slug":"terry-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tom French","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11039","person_slug":"tom-french","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tom Venning","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_11051","person_slug":"tom-venning","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Pasin","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Cook","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11037","person_slug":"trish-cook","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zhi Soon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11049","person_slug":"zhi-soon","vote":"no"}],"name":"Bills — Excise Tariff Amendment (Draught Beer) Bill 2025; Consideration in Detail","noes":81,"question":"Monique Ryan by leave—I move: (1) Schedule 1, heading, page 3 (line 1), omit \"Temporary\", substitute \"Indefinite\". (2) Schedule 1, item 1, page 3 (line 7), omit \"Temporary\", substitute \"Indefinite\". (3) Schedule 1, item 1, page 3 (lines 8 to 19), omit subsection 6L(1), substitute: (1) Despite any other provision of this Act, subsection 6A(1) applies in relation to each CPI indexed draught beer rate as if the indexation factor were 1 for 1 August 2025 or a later indexation day. Note: This means the rates as they are on 31 July 2025 will be unchanged indefinitely. I propose amendments to the Excise Tariff Amendment (Draught Beer) Bill 2025 and Customs Tariff Amendment (Draught Beer) Bill 2025. The rising cost of living has challenged millions of Australian families for several years now, with inflation rising sharply since our economy bounced back after COVID. The government has a hand in setting the price of relatively few grocery items, but one of them is the cost of beer. The average price of draught beer has gone up by over 30 per cent in the last three years, an increase which is considerably higher than the rate of inflation. This has, at least in part, been driven by the automatic indexation of the beer excise every six months which has forced price increases above their annual CPI. This indexation is yet another typical anomaly in our unnecessarily complex tax system. It's pleasing to see the government's commitment to freezing indexation on draught beer for two years, but indexation of the excise over recent years has left those draught beer prices already too high. Indexation of the beer excise needs to stop, and that's why I'm moving that this freeze should be permanent. A permanent cap on the draught beer excise would help millions of Australians with cost-of-living pressures. It would also help support Australia's emerging craft beer industry. Despite rapid growth of small independent brewers, 85 per cent of Australia's beer market is controlled by two fo","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-9849","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2026-02-04/3"}
